<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila pseudoobscura Turing wavelength at 2.0 µm (detail rung, 0 Ma) (Drosophila pseudoobscura)",
        "Drosophila pseudoobscura Turing wavelength at 2.0 µm (detail rung, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Drosophila pseudoobscura morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila pseudoobscura specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila pseudoobscura" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That Richards 2005 measured a reaction-diffusion wavelength.",
        "does_not_claim: That planitibia → pseudoobscura → santomea is a stratigraphic ancestor-descendant series.",
        "does_not_claim: That spacing RMSE = 0 is an independent empirical discovery. The domain was built so twelve critical wavelengths fit exactly, and the saturated stripes lock to that harmonic.",
        "does_not_claim: That the growth GIF is a time-lapse of embryogenesis.",
        "does_not_claim: That the sex comb or the third-chromosome inversions are produced by this 2 µm mode.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Chronoseries comparison: Δlog10 λ versus planitibia is -2.003 and versus santomea is +1.717, with Δage = 0 Ma. Diffusivity would have to be about 10112 times larger to put this Jacobian on the planitibia rung.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Jacobian (0.84, -0.90, 1.55, -1.20) s^-1 and diffusivities D_u = 0.028046, D_v = 0.131825 µm²/s place the fastest mode at 1.961 µm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Split-step integration of σ(k) u - γ u³ with γ = σ_max / 0.35², 320 steps, seed 3200. A weak x-axis orientation weight is a stand-in for the anterior-posterior axis.",
        "reported_in_source: Kopp (2011) reviews sex-comb evolution. The two-segment comb is not a 1.961 µm stripe.",
        "reported_in_source: Richards et al. (2005) sequenced D. pseudoobscura. They do not report a Turing wavelength.",
        "reported_in_source: The Hanson 2019 Commons file is a lateral photograph of an adult male under CC BY-SA 4.0.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) gives the two-species dispersion relation and the conditions for a diffusion-driven band.",
        "transfer_boundary: 1.961e-6 m is the assigned detail rung of this slot, not a published histological period for a D. pseudoobscura ocellus.",
        "transfer_boundary: Planitibia and santomea wavelengths are neighbouring MorphoEval primordium rungs, not measurements made in this script." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila pseudoobscura (North American Obscura-Group Fly)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_pseudoobscura_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif; organism: Drosophila pseudoobscura; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, pillow 13.0.0, matplotlib 3.11.2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) gives the two-species dispersion relation and the conditions for a diffusion-driven band. | Richards et al. (2005) sequenced D. pseudoobscura. They do not report a Turing wavelength. | Kopp (2011) reviews sex-comb evolution. The two-segment comb is not a 1.961 µm stripe. | The Hanson 2019 Commons file is a lateral photograph of an adult male under CC BY-SA 4.0.; reconstructed_in_script: Jacobian (0.84, -0.90, 1.55, -1.20) s^-1 and diffusivities D_u = 0.028046, D_v = 0.131825 µm²/s place the fastest mode at 1.961 µm. | Split-step integration of σ(k) u - γ u³ with γ = σ_max / 0.35², 320 steps, seed 3200. A weak x-axis orientation weight is a stand-in for the anterior-posterior axis. | Chronoseries comparison: Δlog10 λ versus planitibia is -2.003 and versus santomea is +1.717, with Δage = 0 Ma. Diffusivity would have to be about 10112 times larger to put this Jacobian on the planitibia rung.; transfer_boundary: 1.961e-6 m is the assigned detail rung of this slot, not a published histological period for a D. pseudoobscura ocellus. | Planitibia and santomea wavelengths are neighbouring MorphoEval primordium rungs, not measurements made in this script.; does_not_claim: That Richards 2005 measured a reaction-diffusion wavelength. | That the sex comb or the third-chromosome inversions are produced by this 2 µm mode. | That planitibia → pseudoobscura → santomea is a stratigraphic ancestor-descendant series. | That spacing RMSE = 0 is an independent empirical discovery. The domain was built so twelve critical wavelengths fit exactly, and the saturated stripes lock to that harmonic. | That the growth GIF is a time-lapse of embryogenesis.]; other sources: Drosophila pseudoobscura male (File:Dpse_1.tif) <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dpse_1.tif>; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
